   driving behaviour recognition},
Journal = {IET INTELLIGENT TRANSPORT SYSTEMS},
Year = {2020},
Volume = {14},
Number = {5},
Pages = {306-312},
Month = {MAY},
Abstract = {Abnormal driving behaviours, such as rapid acceleration, emergency
   braking, and rapid lane changing, bring great uncertainty to traffic,
   and can easily lead to traffic accidents. The accurate identification of
   abnormal driving behaviour helps to judge the driver's driving style,
   inform surrounding vehicles, and ensure the road traffic safety. Most of
   the existing studies use clustering and shallow learning, it is
   difficult to accurately identify the types of abnormal driving
   behaviours. Aimed at addressing the difficulty of identifying driving
   behaviour, this study proposed a recognition model based on a long
   short-term memory network and convolutional neural network (LSTM-CNN).
   The extreme acceleration and deceleration points are detected through
   the statistical analysis of real vehicle driving data, and the driving
   behaviour recognition data set is established. By using the data set to
   train the model, the LSTM-CNN can achieve a better result.},
